# MCPB Pack Exclusion List
# Rewritten 2026-09-03 - a `just pack` run shipped a 47.6MB / 5328-file bundle including the
# entire web_sota/node_modules/ tree (tailwindcss, typescript, eslint... ~40MB alone), native/
# compiled binaries, .github/, *.egg-info/, and stray .bak files, because this list only
# covered a handful of dev-tooling dirs. Expanded to match what actually leaked through, not
# just a generic template.

tests/
.git/
.github/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
dist/
build/
target/
docs/
scripts/
*.dxt
.cursor/
.windsurf/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.ruff_cache/
Cargo.lock

# mcpb/ is a legacy staging directory not used by the actual `just pack` recipe (which packs
# the repo root directly, entry_point src/vrchat_mcp/server.py) - without this, mcpb/ (its own
# stale mcpb/server/ tree and a previous mcpb/dist/vrchat-mcp.mcpb build artifact) would ship
# nested inside every new package.
mcpb/
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.orig
*.rej

# Webapp dev tree - node_modules alone was the majority of the 47.6MB incident. The webapp is
# not part of the MCP server bundle; the server ships src/vrchat_mcp only.
web_sota/
examples/

# Native/Tauri build tree and its compiled sidecar binaries - not part of the MCP server.
native/

# Python packaging metadata (regenerated by pip/uv, not source)
*.egg-info/

# Legacy dxt packaging leftovers (DXT is retired fleet-wide, see JUNE_2026_STANDARDS_BAR.md)
dxt/
mcpb.json

# Repo/IDE/CI metadata not needed at runtime
.cursorrules
.gitattributes
.snapshots/
llms.txt
llms-full.txt
glama.json

# MCPB_PACKAGING_STANDARDS.md 2.3: pyproject.toml/uv.lock are metadata, not runtime payload
# (uv.lock alone was 432.8kB - by far the largest non-node_modules item in this bundle).
# Rust/Tauri sidecar source - unrelated to the Python MCP server this bundle ships.
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
src/lib.rs
Cargo.toml
start.bat
start.ps1
